  "profileFaqScreenTitle": "FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS",
  "profileFaqQuestion1": "How do I import a character from aidedd.org?",
  "profileFaqAnswer1": "On aidedd.org, open your character sheet and use its XML export (the site's export button). In Nexus JDR, go to Characters > \"+\" > Import an XML file, then select that file. The app automatically pre-fills the sheet (stats, class, race, spells, inventory...) and shows you a review screen before saving it, with any fields it couldn't recognize flagged with a badge so you can fill them in yourself.",
  "profileFaqQuestion2": "How do I join my GM's story?",
  "profileFaqAnswer2": "Your GM shares an invitation code or link from the Histoires app. In Nexus JDR, open that link or enter the code on the \"Join a story\" screen, then choose the character to attach (an existing one or a new one). The character then stays synced with that story until the GM revokes access.",
  "profileFaqQuestion3": "Are my characters saved offline?",
  "profileFaqAnswer3": "Yes. All your characters stay viewable and editable without a connection: changes (hit points, XP, inventory...) are queued on your device and automatically synced with the server as soon as the connection comes back. No data is lost in case of a network outage.",
  "profileFaqQuestion4": "How does leveling up work?",
  "profileFaqAnswer4": "From the character sheet, the \"Level up\" screen guides you step by step: new hit points, unlocked class features, new spell slots if your class casts spells, and an ability score increase if the level allows it. Nothing is applied until you confirm the summary screen.",
  "profileFaqQuestion5": "How do I change my character's portrait?",
  "profileFaqAnswer5": "Open the character sheet, tap its portrait, then choose \"Take a photo\" or \"Choose from gallery\". You can then crop the image before saving it — it's stored securely and linked only to that character.",
  "profileFaqQuestion6": "How do I delete my account?",
  "profileFaqAnswer6": "From Profile > Privacy & data > Delete my account, at the bottom of the screen (danger zone). This action is irreversible: it permanently deletes your characters, their portraits and all links to stories. You can export your data before confirming.",

